{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character","id":1157673,"title":"Simplifying mass combat: Representing a crowd of NPCs as a single \"character\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-10T18:51:38-08:00","id":1157673,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Simplifying mass combat: Representing a crowd of NPCs as a single \"character\"","content":"I'm currently running a Changeling chronicle in which my players rescued the inhabitants of a fae-owned tenement building from a fire, causing everyone they rescued to owe the players a life-debt. In total, there are about 15 NPCs, mostly changelings and a few ensorcelled mortals, who for most intents and purposes act as a single character: the players have to make Social rolls in order to convince the NPCs to do anything that's dangerous or not in their own immediate interests.<br /> <br /> The most recent session ended on a cliffhanger, in which the main baddie and his cronies are trying to burn down the temporary shelter which the players found to house the NPCs, Obviously, the NPCs are going to defend themselves from the bad guys and try to put out the fire, but I <i>really </i>don't want to have to deal with 15 NPCs (not including the bad guys they're fighting against) in a single battle.<br /> <br /> What I'd really like to do instead is <b>find a way to represent a small crowd of NPCs as a single &quot;character&quot;</b><b> with a shared pool of Health and Willpower and a single initiative score.</b> The crowd would act and attack together, and mostly avoid combat but could defend itself if cornered or seriously threatened (these NPCs are not combat specialists, just regular folks who happen to be changelings, or are mortals in relationships with changelings). Any suggestions on how to handle this hypothetical &quot;NPC blob&quot; in combat? As the crowd takes more and more damage, how do I decide when individual NPCs become incapacitated, thereby reducing the blob's dice pools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":6327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","user":"Super_Dave","date":". 11-10-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:52:31-08:00","id":1157681,"title":"","content":"As is, the books have you use a Down and Dirty roll with the group having extra dice based on Teamwork.<br /> <br /> If you want it more drawn out, you can do the same thing, each additional person adding 1 Health and Willpower, successful individual rolls adding to their overall dicepool. Might do something else for Willpower, presumably seeing your allies fall might hurt it more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2017, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T08:44:08-08:00","id":1157761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157681#post1157681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As is, the books have you use a Down and Dirty roll with the group having extra dice based on Teamwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does a &quot;Down and Dirty roll&quot; work, and how would Teamwork affect it? Sorry, I'm not very familiar with 2nd Edition rules; I'm still running my chronicle using 1st Edition. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157681#post1157681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want it more drawn out, you can do the same thing, each additional person adding 1 Health and Willpower, successful individual rolls adding to their overall dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the crowd would have 15 Health boxes and 15 Willpower? That seems like a lot of Willpower, but maybe it would be balanced by the fact that each time the crowd takes a point of lethal damage (or maybe <i>two </i>points of lethal, or three points of bashing, or whatever) the crowd would lose a constituent member (who presumably falls to the ground or runs away and takes cover) and reduce its overall Size, Health, and Willpower pool by one point. At least, that's how I envision it playing out; maybe the math will work out differently once I actually start playtesting this.<br /> <br /> Let me see if I'm understanding the second part of your suggestion: I <i>think </i>you're saying that having an individual in the group who has expertise in a particular field (combat, academics, etc.) would grant the crowd an equipment bonus based on the constituent member's level of expertise? That seems fair to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157681#post1157681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might do something else for Willpower, presumably seeing your allies fall might hurt it more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that just <i>seeing </i>other characters (like the PCs) being harmed might cause the crowd to lose morale (in the form of Willpower points)? That's actually a really cool idea, and one which I'd be willing to implement in my own game. The crowd could easily do a lot more damage than the PCs, so it'd have to be balanced by making them a little fragile, and not letting them outshine the PCs. Maybe the PCs should have to make a Wits + Persuasion roll (or use the &quot;Inspirational&quot; Merit) just to convince the crowd to enter the fray in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:10:45-08:00","id":1157778,"title":"","content":"How about, the &quot;mob&quot; as well will call it has 2 actions. 1 is an automatic attack done against everyone adjacent to the mob and engaged against it, representing the grunts all ganging up on everyone in range. Action 2 is that the mob uses its other abilities, dedicated attacks, thrown weapons, uses guns, uses magical powers shared by the group, done after the first, representing more coordinated action and assault. The first attack would have very little dice, it's more of a passive ability than anything. The second attack has alot more to spend because it is more aggressive that way. Maybe there's 2 or 3 second actions instead of 1 for bigger mobs, it would be better than more dice I feel, because it makes balancing simpler than arbitrarily big numbers for attacking with.<br /> <br /> In any event, the one problem with using Willpower as a resource is that a mob gets really energized from successfully causing damage; it's part of the way mob mentality works. Perhaps as the caveat to how the mob works, all successful actions restore 1 point of Willpower to the mob, but failing actions demoralizes them such failing to land hits depletes willpower: Such as say 1 turn of failing to land any damage drains willpower, but also failing any rolls boosted using Willpower hurts because the mob literally gave it their best but still fails.<br /> <br /> Some traits and other actions can be added too, suicidal zeal would be represented by the mob self damaging itself for more dice. Zombies obviously would lack willpower, but don't restore it by causing damage or break from being low on Willpower/ Morale.<br /> <br /> Rally and Triage could also be actions, representing people spending time getting allies back into the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 11-11-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:58:05-08:00","id":1157785,"title":"","content":"This is a battle group from Exalted 3e. That's literally what you're trying to make here, but with Chronicles rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:04:06-08:00","id":1157789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157761#post1157761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a &quot;Down and Dirty roll&quot; work, and how would Teamwork affect it? Sorry, I'm not very familiar with 2nd Edition rules; I'm still running my chronicle using 1st Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I'm sorry, I should have guessed with the Changeling thing. Basically Down and Dirty is for single roll combat. It can be used to just skip over lengthy combat scenes or show how much one side dominates.<br /> <br /> Take the leader of the mob's Strength + Brawl as a dicepool, the leader would be called the primary actor. Then roll everyone else in the mob individually (you only have to do this once) for their Strength + Brawl. You can use other dicepools if you're trying to get them to build a house or put out an inferno. Everyone else's roll doesn't just add to the primary actor, I think this was to keep groups from just steamrolling things, but it also acts to simulate the 'too many cooks in the kitchen' effect, where people are getting in each others way if they haven't trained to work as a team. Each actor who succeeds on their roll adds 1 die to the primary actor's dicepool. That's just the Teamwork part.<br /> <br /> Down and Dirty roll would then have that primary actor's adjusted dicepool versus the similar dicepool of the character confronting them (also potentially adjusted by teamwork bonuses). Whoever gets more successes wins the combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the crowd would have 15 Health boxes and 15 Willpower? That seems like a lot of Willpower, but maybe it would be balanced by the fact that each time the crowd takes a point of lethal damage (or maybe <i>two </i>points of lethal, or three points of bashing, or whatever) the crowd would lose a constituent member (who presumably falls to the ground or runs away and takes cover) and reduce its overall Size, Health, and Willpower pool by one point. At least, that's how I envision it playing out; maybe the math will work out differently once I actually start playtesting this. </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I'm understanding the second part of your suggestion: I <i>think </i>you're saying that having an individual in the group who has expertise in a particular field (combat, academics, etc.) would grant the crowd an equipment bonus based on the constituent member's level of expertise? That seems fair to me.[/quote]<br /> <br /> That's a way to do it too, I meant the Teamwork thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you saying that just <i>seeing </i>other characters (like the PCs) being harmed might cause the crowd to lose morale (in the form of Willpower points)? That's actually a really cool idea, and one which I'd be willing to implement in my own game. The crowd could easily do a lot more damage than the PCs, so it'd have to be balanced by making them a little fragile, and not letting them outshine the PCs. Maybe the PCs should have to make a Wits + Persuasion roll (or use the &quot;Inspirational&quot; Merit) just to convince the crowd to enter the fray in the first place? </div> </div> </div>Ooh that's a good way to handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T12:41:45-08:00","id":1157805,"title":"","content":"Give a crowd a Power, Finesse and Resistance attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T13:55:41-08:00","id":1157813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157805#post1157805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give a crowd a Power, Finesse and Resistance attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Example on how to do this? I'd really like to know and it seems like a solid method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T14:53:46-08:00","id":1157818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157813#post1157813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Example on how to do this? I'd really like to know and it seems like a solid method.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Power = Attack dice<br /> Finesse = Defense, possibly ranged attack dice (defense on a really large group of bodifes to me makes no sense)<br /> Resiliance = Health/Morale<br /> <br /> And then add in the variation from supernatural powers or other tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T16:12:28-08:00","id":1157826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157818#post1157818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Power = Attack dice<br /> Finesse = Defense, possibly ranged attack dice (defense on a really large group of bodifes to me makes no sense)<br /> Resiliance = Health/Morale<br /> <br /> And then add in the variation from supernatural powers or other tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T16:22:40-08:00","id":1157830,"title":"","content":"The Chronicles of Darkness book stats up a crowd of zombies using the Brief Nightmare rules, no reason you can't use the same rules for things which aren't actually monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T23:52:03-08:00","id":1157889,"title":"","content":"If you need slightly more nuanced rules from advice made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> - I advice my created <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857534-dark-eras-battle-mass-combat-rules\">Mass Combat rules</a> based on Brief Nightmares mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I checked it already to run Vikings war party attacking Christians monastery in 799 A.D. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T02:33:12-08:00","id":1157898,"title":"","content":"Eh, that more complicates combat IMO. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T05:55:54-08:00","id":1157914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157818#post1157818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Power = Attack dice<br /> Finesse = Defense, possibly ranged attack dice (defense on a really large group of bodifes to me makes no sense)<br /> Resiliance = Health/Morale<br /> <br /> And then add in the variation from supernatural powers or other tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> I hope it is not too much to ask how to do it though. How would you calculate exactly how many die the group would get? How do I know how many die to give a platoon of veteran soldiers, a drunken bar mob or a myriad of children?<br /> Would I just take the highest skilled individual and give +1 to one or more of the three stats for each extra person in the group?<br /> <br /> How do I simulate the loss of individuals (Health) to the group? Do I just reduce their stats for each individual lost and also have them do a Res (Morale) roll for the group not to disband after each hit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T06:09:10-08:00","id":1157916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157914#post1157914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> I hope it is not too much to ask how to do it though. How would you calculate exactly how many die the group would get? How do I know how many die to give a platoon of veteran soldiers, a drunken bar mob or a myriad of children?<br /> Would I just take the highest skilled individual and give +1 to one or more of the three stats for each extra person in the group?<br /> <br /> How do I simulate the loss of individuals (Health) to the group? Do I just reduce their stats for each individual lost and also have them do a Res (Morale) roll for the group not to disband after each hit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do averages (After modifiers) for attack, 3 dice means 1s on average, 6 means 2s, etc.<br /> <br /> Do your players have an average defense of 5/6? Are they facing an elite anti riot police force with military equipment head on? give the cops power 20. They're likely hampered in the Finesse department with all the armor, so give them a 5 there and say 15 health levels/resistance<br /> <br /> If you need to roll an individual person's resistance because say, Dominate or equivalent, there's relevant combatant stats you can use in the books for that.<br /> <br /> If you're making a crowd, each damage they take is either someone who loss commitment to the cause or gets arrested or becomes a casualty (or it's simply too bruised to get up again). Someone spraying autofire into the crow is likely to disperse and decimate it far more easily than trying to reason with it with rhetoric.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that harming/demoralizing several people at once is more than likely a breaking point to most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 11-12-2017, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T07:44:00-08:00","id":1157930,"title":"","content":"You can also check the optional rules for Beaten Down (CofD, pg 87). If Health lost to the mob represent members getting taken out, then suffering casualties could easily result in the mob breaking up.<br /> <br /> [Optional]<br /> For more resilience, have them roll Resistance (+ modifiers, like good morale, being inspired, defending themselves) - penalties (damage taken, fearsome opponents, etc.). Success = no consequence; Exceptional Success = they get fired up even more and gain 1 Willpower, or get a Condition like Inspired, or something; Failure = Spend 1 Willpower or downgrade to Dramatic Failure; Dramatic Failure = suffer Beaten Down (or just disperse);","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T01:49:16-08:00","id":1159366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1157916#post1157916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do averages (After modifiers) for attack, 3 dice means 1s on average, 6 means 2s, etc.<br /> <br /> Do your players have an average defense of 5/6? Are they facing an elite anti riot police force with military equipment head on? give the cops power 20. They're likely hampered in the Finesse department with all the armor, so give them a 5 there and say 15 health levels/resistance<br /> <br /> If you need to roll an individual person's resistance because say, Dominate or equivalent, there's relevant combatant stats you can use in the books for that.<br /> <br /> If you're making a crowd, each damage they take is either someone who loss commitment to the cause or gets arrested or becomes a casualty (or it's simply too bruised to get up again). Someone spraying autofire into the crow is likely to disperse and decimate it far more easily than trying to reason with it with rhetoric.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that harming/demoralizing several people at once is more than likely a breaking point to most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, would this be a correct way?<br /> <br /> 5 thugs in a bar fight<br /> Average Power 1, Finesse 1, Resistance 1<br /> =<br /> Pow 5<br /> Finesse 5<br /> Resistance 5<br /> <br /> 5 gangster enforcers<br /> Average Power 2, Finesse 2, Resistance 2<br /> =<br /> Power 10<br /> Finesse 10<br /> Resistance 10<br /> <br /> Also: how would you treat Willpower for the mob? One WP per individual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T12:58:31-08:00","id":1159525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157673-simplifying-mass-combat-representing-a-crowd-of-npcs-as-a-single-character?p=1159366#post1159366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, would this be a correct way?<br /> <br /> 5 thugs in a bar fight<br /> Average Power 1, Finesse 1, Resistance 1<br /> =<br /> Pow 5<br /> Finesse 5<br /> Resistance 5<br /> <br /> 5 gangster enforcers<br /> Average Power 2, Finesse 2, Resistance 2<br /> =<br /> Power 10<br /> Finesse 10<br /> Resistance 10<br /> <br /> Also: how would you treat Willpower for the mob? One WP per individual?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would divide by 3. So, treating Thug #1 as the primary, with 4 equal supports, you'd get Power 2, etc. For the enforcers, 2 + (2 Power * 4 Extra Members = 8 / 3 = 2, rounded down, 3, rounded up) so 4 or 5.<br /> <br /> Power of 1 and 2 is still really low for the individuals. Basically Strength 1, no skill (but no untrained penalty). For average combatants, I'd say the starting point should be 3 or 4 (Average Strength/Power of 2, with 1 Skill in their attack of choice, 2 if they are more focus/active). You can increase from there as the situation warrants.<br /> <br /> For Willpower, you could do the same - highest Res+Com or Resistance + sum of the helpers / 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T16:03:28-08:00","id":1159607,"title":"","content":"Why do you need 1:1 multiplication for people power? Why not use a special group size modifier to give a general idea of how big the group is, because past the first handful each additional person contributes less to the group overall for each additional unit, essentially, the principal of depreciation or diminishing returns would kick in.<br /> <br /> It also saves on recalculating for when adjusting for casualities or for groups made up of huge or extremely short people. Just use conditions to represent casualties instead of recalculating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 11-16-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:16:18-08:00","id":1159629,"title":"","content":"Personally, you can just use a Horde Brief Nightmare and just spit-ball the dice pools for what you need. Figure out how dangerous that group <i>should</i> be, and then design the dice pools around that. Take a second glance and see if it reasonable, or needs adjustment (or justification).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T06:58:52-08:00","id":1160838,"title":"","content":"Awesome suggestions, everyone! I've consolidated all the suggestions into what I <i>think</i> is a workable prototype. Here, take a look and tell me what you think.<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mob Rules, World of Darkness</span></u><br /> <i>Combining large groups into a single, simulated \u201ccharacter\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The simplest way to run mass combat is to boil the constituent characters\u2019 stats down into three core Attributes (as per Spirits and Ghosts):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Power</b> = Attack dice [equal to the average constituent character\u2019s highest Power Attribute]<br /> <b>Finesse</b> = Defense (only against Weaponry and Brawl attacks), Ranged attack dice [equal to the average constituent character\u2019s highest Finesse Attribute]<br /> <b>Resistance</b> = Health/Morale [equal to the average constituent character\u2019s highest Resistance Attribute]</div> <b>Health</b>: equal to the total number of constituent characters, plus the Mob\u2019s Resistance Attribute.<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: a mob has one point of Willpower per member, up to a maximum of [average constituent character\u2019s Willpower].<br /> <b>Speed</b>: Equal to three-quarters of the average constituent character\u2019s Speed (rounded down).<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: Equal to the average constituent character\u2019s Finesse. A Mob acts as a single character in combat, occupying a single Initiative slot and making one unified attack (usually Power + Finesse) against a given character (or another Mob) per turn.<br /> <b>Armor</b>: applies only if more than half the Mob's constituent characters are wearing armor.<br /> <br /> After calculating the Mob\u2019s Attributes, then add variations or bonuses from supernatural powers or other tricks (e.g., increased Power for vampires, increased Finesse for mages, increased Resistance for werewolves, etc.)<br /> Relevant training or tools can add equipment bonuses to a Mob\u2019s dice pools.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Special Mob Abilities</b></u>:<ul><li><u><b>Mayhem</b></u>: In addition to this single attack per turn, a Mob deals an automatic point of Bashing damage (or Lethal damage, if armed) to every character, object, or structure at \u201cengaged\u201d range (i.e., standing directly next to the Mob) at the end of its turn. This damage <i>can </i>be overcome by damage resistance and armor.</li> <li><u><b>Surround</b></u>: As a full-round action, a Mob may surround and absorb a single character into its mass and deal a number of points of automatic Bashing damage (or Lethal, if armed) at the end of its turn to the absorbed character; this attack deals a number of damage points equal to the Mob\u2019s Power (the Mob still deals its normal automatic Bashing damage to all other characters who are at \u201cengaged\u201d range at the end of the Mob\u2019s turn. To escape, the surrounded character may (on his or her turn) make an instant and contested <b>Strength + Athletics/Brawl</b> roll vs. the Mob\u2019s <b>Strength + Resistance</b> roll.</li> </ul><br /> Each point of damage which a Mob takes represents a constituent character who lost commitment to the cause, got arrested/taken down, was killed, or became too bruised to get up again. (i.e., someone spraying autofire into the Mob is likely to disperse and decimate it far more easily than trying to reason with it with rhetoric). When half of a Mob\u2019s Health boxes are full, have the Mob roll its <b>Resistance + morale modifiers \u2013 morale penalties</b> (for damage taken, fearsome opponents, etc.)<br /> <b>Roll results</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b> = the Mob gains the \u201cBeaten Down\u201d Condition, or simply disperses (at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion)<br /> <b>Failure</b> = Lose 1 Willpower or downgrade to Dramatic Failure;<br /> <b>Success</b> = no consequence;<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b> = they get fired up even more and gain 1 Willpower, or gain a Condition (such as Inspired, etc.)</div> <br /> <b>NB: </b>harming/demoralizing several people at once <i>may count as a breaking point </i>to most people.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Mobs: </b><br /> 5 thugs in a bar fight (Avg. Power 1, Avg. Finesse 1, Avg. Resistance 1) = Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 5, Speed 10, Health 10, Initiative 1<br /> 5 gangster enforcers (Avg. Power 2, Avg. Finesse 2, Avg. Resistance 2) = Power 10, Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Speed 12, Health 15, Initiative 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"us